<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <div>
      <span class="price-badge">Every template <span>$5</span></span>
      <h1 class="mt-3">Good website templates<br>shouldn't cost $79.</h1>
      <p class="lede mt-2">
        <%= total %> hand-built templates. Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript — no build step, no framework
        to learn, no subscription. Answer five questions and we'll tell you which one fits.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__actions">
        <a class="btn btn--accent btn--lg" href="/find">Find my template</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/templates">Browse all <%= total %></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__proof">
        <div><b><%= total %></b><span>templates</span></div>
        <div><b>$5</b><span>flat, one time</span></div>
        <div><b>3 for $12</b><span>bundle price</span></div>
        <div><b>&infin;</b><span>re-downloads</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card card--raised" style="padding:0;overflow:hidden">
      <div style="padding:18px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
        <span class="eyebrow">The guided finder</span>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Five questions, about forty seconds. You get ranked matches with the reasons for each — and what each one is missing.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:20px">
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step"><span class="step__num"></span><div><b>What are you building?</b><p class="small muted">Store, portfolio, restaurant, SaaS, blog, agency.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step"><span class="step__num"></span><div><b>Selling anything?</b><p class="small muted">Decides catalogue vs. booking vs. neither.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step"><span class="step__num"></span><div><b>Which features matter?</b><p class="small muted">We show the gaps rather than hide them.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn--block mt-3" href="/find">Start &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row row--between section-head" style="max-width:none;align-items:flex-end">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The catalogue</span>
        <h2 class="mt-1">Fewer templates, each one finished</h2>
        <p>Every one is responsive, keyboard-accessible, and ships with its own README.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/templates">See all <%= total %></a>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <% featured.forEach(function (template) { %>
        <%- include('../partials/template-card', { template }) %>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center" style="margin-inline:auto">
      <span class="eyebrow">What $5 actually buys</span>
      <h2 class="mt-1">The whole thing, permanently</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Full source</h3>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Every HTML file, the stylesheet, the JavaScript, the images. Nothing minified, nothing obfuscated, no licence key phoning home.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>A licence that isn't a trap</h3>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Use it for one site, commercial or not. Modify it however you like. Hand it to a client as paid work. You just can't resell the template itself. <a href="/licence">Read it</a> — it's 200 words.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Re-download forever</h3>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Your account keeps every template you've bought. New laptop, lost folder, three years later — it's still there.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Tutorials that go all the way</h3>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Not "here's how to unzip a file". How to deploy it, point a domain at it, wire the contact form, and put a real Stripe checkout behind the cart. <a href="/tutorials">Read them</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>A domain, found for you</h3>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Tell the <a href="/domains">domain finder</a> what you're building and it ranks names that are actually registrable — not the bare dictionary words every other tool suggests.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>No account needed to buy</h3>
        <p class="small muted mt-1">Check out as a guest with just an email. We create the account behind it so your download link keeps working; set a password whenever you feel like it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="container container--narrow center">
    <h2>Pick one in under a minute</h2>
    <p class="lede mt-2" style="margin-inline:auto">The finder asks five questions and ranks the catalogue against your answers — showing why each one matched and what it's missing.</p>
    <div class="row mt-3" style="justify-content:center">
      <a class="btn btn--accent btn--lg" href="/find">Find my template</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/templates">Just show me everything</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
